{
  "id": "COMPOUND:28471 - PROTEIN:5798",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but interconnected pathway linking (22R,25R)-spirosolan-3beta-ol to NH-6 through multiple targets. The drug is identified as a target of several enzymes in the SDR family, including Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which in turn targets 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol. This enzyme is also a target of 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, which ultimately leads to NH-6. The shared involvement of these enzymes in the metabolic pathway indicates a potential mechanism where (22R,25R)-spirosolan-3beta-ol may act as a substrate or inhibitor of these enzymes, thereby influencing NH-6. The evidence supports a dependency on these metabolic pathways, suggesting that the drug may exert its effects through a mechanism involving enzyme inhibition or modulation. The integration of these targets highlights a possible role in the regulation of NH-6 through a network of enzymatic interactions.",
